# Everything here is excluded from the build context. Two reasons it matters:
# the context is transferred on every build, and — more importantly — any file
# that reaches the context can invalidate a cached layer. Before this list, a
# one-line edit to a runbook or a Claude skill forced a full `next build` on
# the VPS, because the `build` stage used a blanket `COPY . .`.
#
# The Dockerfile now copies only the build inputs explicitly, so this file is
# a second line of defence rather than the only one — but it still keeps the
# transferred context small (468 tracked files, of which ~3.6 MB is .claude).

.git
.github
.worktrees
.claude
node_modules
.next
RAW
data
docs

# Test and lint sources: never needed to build or run the image.
# `scripts/` is deliberately NOT here — the `tools` stage ships it so an
# operator can run `npm run user:create` / `images:import` in the container.
# It reaches only that stage; the `build` stage copies neither it nor tests.
tests
coverage
vitest.config.ts
eslint.config.mjs

# Secrets never enter the image; real values come from the container env_file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
